meta {
  name: Fetch Meta Campaigns
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/meta/campaigns/sync?tenant_id={{tenantId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

docs {
  The "Fetch campaigns" button. Walks every ad account in
  ext.meta_tenant_config.ad_account_ids for the SELECTED tenant, cursor-paged,
  and upserts ext.meta_campaigns.

  Returns { fetched, inserted, suggested, unmapped, confirmed_untouched, errors }.

  Requires super_admin and an explicit ?tenant_id=: the call spends that
  tenant's stored Meta credentials. The token needs `ads_read` — without it
  every account fails with Meta #200 and comes back in `errors` rather than
  throwing, so a partial run is still reported honestly.

  Regression checks:
    * run it TWICE. The second run must report inserted: 0 and change nothing.
    * confirm a campaign (see Confirm-Meta-Campaign.bru), then re-run. Its
      campaign_type_id, mapping_status and confirmed_by must be untouched while
      name, effective_status and last_synced_at refresh. This is the phase's
      core invariant — a confirmed mapping is NEVER overwritten.
    * add a keyword to a campaign type, re-run: `suggested` and `unmapped` rows
      re-match; `confirmed` rows do not move.
    * tenant with no integration, or an inactive one -> 404
    * tenant with an empty ad_account_ids           -> 404 naming the column
    * caller below super_admin                      -> 403
    * a 429 from Meta must back off and retry, not fail the whole run — look for
      evt: campaign_sync.graph_backoff in the service log.
}
